FILAMENT APOCALYPSE

(15 seconds · 8K UHD · 30 fps · 2.39:1 · Surreal Mythic Realism)

ANCHOR / PLAYGROUND (0.3–0.5s)

A mythic trio of wild lions walking forward in perfect formation across dry golden grass.
Their manes and bodies are composed of layered filament-paint strands, thick and tactile, like flowing oil paint pulled into threads.
The sky behind them is a towering mass of woven clouds, made of pastel filaments—teal, cyan, magenta, rose, gold—braided like fabric under tension.
Lighting is cinematic sunset: warm horizon glow, cool cyan shadows, high contrast, painterly depth.

STYLE & VISUAL LANGUAGE

Hyper-detailed filament realism · flowing paint-thread physics · mythic symbolism
No cartoon stylization · no flat shading · heavy material presence
Every surface feels woven, pulled, stretched

NARRATIVE ARC

Calm → Unraveling → Collapse → Silence

ENVIRONMENT PHYSICS

The sky is not vapor — it is a woven filament membrane
Wind tension causes sky-threads to stretch, twist, and snap
Filament strands peel from clouds like torn fabric
Horizon layers unravel vertically, exposing nothingness behind
Grass briefly frays into threads as shockwaves pass, then settles

CHARACTER MOTION
Lions walk forward slow, steady, unbothered
Muscles shift beneath filament layers
Manes ripple subtly but never break
Eyes calm, focused, timeless
They do not react to the collapsing world

